# Ignore all files except the following and their contents
*

# Folders and their metas
# NOTE: each folder needs both `!Folder` and `!Folder/**`. Unity 6's Package
# Manager stopped using npm-packlist for git installs and now applies strict
# gitignore semantics, where a path under an excluded directory can never be
# re-included. Without the bare `!Folder` line, `*` excludes the directory
# itself and everything inside stays unreachable, so a git install produces
# empty folders.
!/Runtime
!/Runtime/**
!/Runtime.meta
!/Assets
!/Assets/**
!/Assets.meta
!/Plugins
!/Plugins/**
!/Plugins.meta
!/Resources
!/Resources/**
!/Resources.meta
!/Editor
!/Editor/**
!/Editor.meta

# Top level files which should be included
!/package.json
!/package.json.meta
!/LICENSE
!/LICENSE.meta
!/README.md
!/README.md.meta

# Ignore all folders and files starting with dot
.*

# Other files that should be ignored
*.pdb
*.pdb.meta
*.tgz
*.tgz.meta
